// @@@ For all non-negative integer indices i, if bitIndex is not equal to i and i is within the range of the current length of the BitSet, the value of the bit at index i in the current BitSet should be the same as the value of the bit at index i in the old BitSet.

--------------------
// @@@ For every bit index greater than or equal to 0, for all indices i where 0 <= i < the length of the BitSet and i is not equal to the bit index, the value of the bit at index i is the same as the value of the bit at index i in the previous state of the BitSet.

--------------------
// @@@ For every bit index greater than or equal to 0, for all indices i that are within the range of the length of the BitSet and i is not equal to the bit index, the bit at index i remains the same as before the operation.

